// Class A, the other trigger and a different way of naming it. `String` pulls the
// same two lines in the reference, and the type is named in a PARAMETER rather
// than in a trait signature - so the rule is about the name reaching the typed
// program, not about impls.
//
// One shape is a lower bound: two triggers measured, and the four prelude types
// that do NOT trigger it (Arena, Allocator, Vec, HashMap) stay out of this
// directory because they agree already.
fn width(s: *const String) -> int { return 1; }

fn main() {
    println(width(null as *const String));
}
